00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:06.776
- [Voiceover] Terrell asks,

00:05:06.776 --> 00:05:08.402
"How would you manage pro bono work

00:05:08.402 --> 00:05:10.131
"versus getting paid as a startup,

00:05:10.131 --> 00:05:12.981
"or how do you draw the
line between the two?"

00:05:12.981 --> 00:05:15.709
- I think the question, I
think what I'm getting from it

00:05:15.709 --> 00:05:17.368
is, you know, how do you

00:05:17.368 --> 00:05:20.202
manage the people asking
you do to stuff on spec?

00:05:20.202 --> 00:05:21.804
And it's funny, we've
had some conversations,

00:05:21.804 --> 00:05:25.646
I'm a fan of spec, because
I think it's a gateway drug

00:05:25.646 --> 00:05:28.188
into showing work.

00:05:28.188 --> 00:05:29.547
When you're at zero,

00:05:29.547 --> 00:05:31.288
when you have no track record,

00:05:31.288 --> 00:05:33.895
when you have no leverage,

00:05:33.895 --> 00:05:37.598
spec is a tremendous
opportunity, it's, you're at bat.

00:05:37.598 --> 00:05:42.598
And so, spec has always been
interesting in design work

00:05:42.614 --> 00:05:44.170
or other things of that nature.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:47.489
Any time I even allude to a
spec interplay on Twitter,

00:05:47.489 --> 00:05:49.055
I get attacked, right?

00:05:49.055 --> 00:05:50.438
Like, if I want free t-shirts

00:05:50.438 --> 00:05:52.029
for the Great Wall of Wine Deals,

00:05:52.029 --> 00:05:54.977
right, stickers, why
don't you pay for them?

00:05:54.977 --> 00:05:56.277
I'm thrilled to pay.

00:05:56.277 --> 00:05:57.914
As a matter of fact, in my later years,

00:05:57.914 --> 00:06:00.016
AKA in the last three years,
I've learned, actually,

00:06:00.016 --> 00:06:02.117
I'd rather pay than what I deal with

00:06:02.117 --> 00:06:03.951
when somebody gives you,
like, a sticker for free

00:06:03.951 --> 00:06:07.434
and they want, like, so, I'm into paying.

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:11.392
I actually, when I do these
spec things, look at it as

00:06:11.392 --> 00:06:15.526
the first opportunity to
somebody to have in at bat,

00:06:15.526 --> 00:06:17.093
to, like, change the course of their game.

00:06:17.093 --> 00:06:20.389
We've alluded this question-answer
with DRock in the past,

00:06:20.389 --> 00:06:21.932
like, this is just real to me.

00:06:21.932 --> 00:06:24.313
So where do you draw the line is,

00:06:24.313 --> 00:06:27.087
when you stop thinking
it brings you value.

00:06:27.087 --> 00:06:30.432
By the way, nobody's forcing
you into doing pro bono work.

00:06:30.432 --> 00:06:33.344
Hey, DRock, you wanna make a film with me?

00:06:33.344 --> 00:06:35.190
You should do it, I'm not gonna
pay you, you should do it.

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:37.953
I didn't force him, like,
you know, that's on you.

00:06:37.953 --> 00:06:41.030
So this notion of pro
bono work being, like,

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:43.572
some sort of forced behavior that like,

00:06:43.572 --> 00:06:46.951
the rich are forcing the
poor to do this work,

00:06:46.951 --> 00:06:50.049
in a world where you
should always do everything

00:06:50.049 --> 00:06:52.070
predicated on what brings you value,

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:54.415
including when you bring
other people value.

00:06:54.415 --> 00:06:56.783
See, the dirty little secret is, for me,

00:06:56.783 --> 00:07:00.220
this 51-49 thing where I
wanna do all these things,

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:01.984
it makes me feel good.

00:07:01.984 --> 00:07:03.446
It might not make me more money,

00:07:03.446 --> 00:07:05.327
it makes me feel good.

00:07:05.327 --> 00:07:06.846
It's a selfish act.

00:07:06.846 --> 00:07:08.624
People say that, you
know, you hear it's like,

00:07:08.624 --> 00:07:10.981
oh, it's a selfless
act, like, I understand.

00:07:10.981 --> 00:07:12.966
I like the way it feels.

00:07:12.966 --> 00:07:15.137
And so, you know, your pro bono work

00:07:15.137 --> 00:07:16.483
might be because you wanna use it

00:07:16.483 --> 00:07:19.084
as a gateway drug to business
opportunities in the future,

00:07:19.084 --> 00:07:21.557
or you just might like the way it feels.

00:07:21.557 --> 00:07:23.041
That's on you.

00:07:23.041 --> 00:07:25.643
But, you know, business is simple,

00:07:25.643 --> 00:07:27.361
